{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/matters-A2.json docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/libraries-A2.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"name\": \"NVIDIA's credit-support obligations to AI cloud partners (capacity backstops, rent-back and lease guarantees) as reported in its FY2027 annual report\",\n  \"example_question\": \"How large will NVIDIA's credit-support obligations to AI cloud partners (guarantees and commitments to buy or rent back unsold GPU capacity) be in its FY2027 annual report (fiscal year ending January 2027)?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   1,\n   4,\n   6,\n   7,\n   8,\n   10,\n   11,\n   17,\n   19\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"both\",\n  \"matter\": \"M01\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"Whether NVIDIA signs a financial guarantee for OpenAI's Ohio data center lease by 2027-12-31\",\n  \"example_question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI's lease of the large Ohio data center by 2027-12-31?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   1\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"both\",\n  \"matter\": \"M02\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"Combined 2026 capital expenditures of the largest AI hyperscalers (about $650 billion planned)\",\n  \"example_question\": \"What will the combined 2026 capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers be (about $650 billion planned)?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   12,\n   27,\n   34,\n   35\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"both\",\n  \"matter\": \"M03\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"Combined 2027 capital expenditures of the largest AI hyperscalers (whether they reach $1 trillion)\",\n  \"example_question\": \"Will the four largest AI hyperscalers' combined 2027 capital expenditures reach $1 trillion?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   12,\n   34,\n   35\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"both\",\n  \"matter\": \"M04\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping Vera Rubin Ultra in the Kyber NVL144 rack by 2027-12-31 or slips to 2028\",\n  \"example_question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping Vera Rubin Ultra in the Kyber NVL144 rack by 2027-12-31, or has it slipped to 2028?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   15,\n   18,\n   20,\n   21,\n   22,\n   23,\n   24,\n   25,\n   27,\n   38\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"both\",\n  \"matter\": \"M05\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"Whether China formally approves its companies' purchases of NVIDIA H200 chips by 2027-01-31\",\n  \"example_question\": \"Will China formally approve its companies' purchases of NVIDIA H200 chips by 2027-01-31 (end of NVIDIA's fiscal 2027; reviewer-set check date)?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   36,\n   37,\n   40\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"both\",\n  \"matter\": \"M06\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping Vera Rubin systems to customers by 2026-12-31\",\n  \"example_question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping Vera Rubin platform systems to customers by 2026-12-31?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   14,\n   15,\n   23,\n   24,\n   36\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"both\",\n  \"matter\": \"M07\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"NVIDIA stand-alone CPU revenue in FY2027\",\n  \"example_question\": \"How much stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   14,\n   39\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"one reader\",\n  \"matter\": \"M08\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"U.S. restrictions on Chinese-made lidar\",\n  \"example_question\": \"Will the United States enact restrictions phasing out Chinese-made lidar by 2027-01-31?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   30\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"one reader\",\n  \"matter\": \"M09\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"NVIDIA data center revenue for fiscal 2027 (year ending January 2027)\",\n  \"example_question\": \"What will NVIDIA's data center revenue be for fiscal 2027 (year ending January 2027), against consensus of about 82% total revenue growth?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   12,\n   14,\n   15,\n   17,\n   24,\n   38,\n   39\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"one reader\",\n  \"matter\": \"M10\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"NVIDIA data center revenue for fiscal 2028 (year ending January 2028)\",\n  \"example_question\": \"What will NVIDIA's data center revenue be for fiscal 2028 (year ending January 2028), against consensus of about 41% revenue growth?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   12,\n   38\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"one reader\",\n  \"matter\": \"M11\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"Change in average DRAM contract prices in calendar 2027 versus 2026\",\n  \"example_question\": \"Will average DRAM contract prices in calendar 2027 be higher than in 2026?\",\n  \"articles\": [\n   34\n  ],\n  \"listed_by\": \"one reader\",\n  \"matter\": \"M12\"\n }\n]{\n \"X\": [\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-1\",\n   \"question\": \"How much credit support or guarantee exposure will NVIDIA have signed for AI cloud partners under its new revenue-sharing and credit-support model by 2027-12-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The amount of signed credit-support, guarantee, or similar credit-enhancement commitments NVIDIA discloses for AI cloud partners under the new model.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-12-31 (check date within 18 months of the 2026-07-01 item, for an unsigned obligation)\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 4 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-2\",\n   \"question\": \"How much equity will NVIDIA hold in Intel, and at what total committed amount, at NVIDIA's next annual report, following its $5 billion equity investment in Intel?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The size and carrying amount of NVIDIA's equity stake in Intel, and any additional commitment, disclosed at NVIDIA's next annual report.\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, expected early 2027); the investment is already undertaken, so it is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 2 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-3\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin AI chip platform begin shipping by the end of calendar 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"First shipments of Vera Rubin to customers, confirmed by NVIDIA.\",\n   \"period\": \"2026-12-31 (the item says shipping could begin later in 2026, from a 2026-07-02 article)\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-4\",\n   \"question\": \"Will China's government permit NVIDIA to sell its H200 AI chips to Chinese customers, lifting its current block, by NVIDIA's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A Chinese government/regulator decision allowing H200 sales in China, evidenced by an official Chinese decision or by NVIDIA-confirmed H200 shipments/revenue to Chinese customers.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-01-31 (NVIDIA's current fiscal year-end; set because the item reports a pending regulatory decision with no date of its own)\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-5\",\n   \"question\": \"Will the U.S. Commerce Department conclude its investigation into whether DeepSeek accessed restricted Nvidia AI chips and announce penalties or new export-control measures by NVIDIA's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A U.S. Commerce Department/Bureau of Industry and Security finding, penalty, or new export-control measure stemming from the investigation into DeepSeek's access to restricted Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-01-31 (NVIDIA's current fiscal year-end; set because the item reports a pending regulatory investigation with no date of its own)\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-6\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend in combined data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The sum of calendar-2026 data center capex actually reported by the big four AI hyperscalers, versus the roughly $650 billion they are reported to plan for this year.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; settled by the four hyperscalers' full-year 2026 capex disclosures in their Q4 2026 earnings reports (January–February 2027), the release date of the quantity.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 12 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-7\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system begin shipping to customers by the end of calendar 2028, following SemiAnalysis's report that its debut slipped from 2027 to 2028 (which NVIDIA disputes, saying its roadmap is intact)?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"First customer shipments of the Kyber rack-scale architecture (NVL144) with Vera Rubin Ultra, confirmed by NVIDIA.\",\n   \"period\": \"2028-12-31 (the item says the Kyber debut was pushed to 2028 from a 2027 plan; the check date is the end of that year. If NVIDIA's 'roadmap is intact,' shipping in 2027 would also settle the by-end-2028 question affirmatively.)\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 15 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-8\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the big four AI hyperscalers spend in combined data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027, versus NVIDIA management's forecast that hyperscaler spending will top $1 trillion?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The sum of calendar-2027 data center capex actually reported by the big four AI hyperscalers, compared with the over-$1-trillion figure NVIDIA management forecast for 2027.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; settled by the four hyperscalers' full-year 2027 capex disclosures in their Q4 2027 earnings reports (January–February 2028), the release date of the quantity.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-9\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will NVIDIA have outstanding in supply/purchase commitments at its next annual report?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount of NVIDIA's supply commitments (purchase and capacity commitments) disclosed in its FY2027 Form 10-K, versus the $119 billion cited in this item.\",\n   \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, expected early 2027); the commitments are already undertaken, so they are tracked by their amount at the next annual report.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-10\",\n   \"question\": \"What share of Chinese companies' AI accelerator spending will go to domestic suppliers over the 12 months following July 2026, versus the 46% planned in the Bloomberg Intelligence survey?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The realized share of Chinese enterprises' AI accelerator budget captured by domestic suppliers (Huawei, Hygon, Cambricon and others) over the 12 months from mid-2026, measured against the 46% planned and the 30% current level.\",\n   \"period\": \"The 12 months from the survey's release on 2026-07-07 (to mid-2027); settled when follow-up survey or market-share data covering that period are published.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-11\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will NVIDIA have invested in Firmus Technologies, and what equity stake will it hold, following its reported ~$500 million ($721 million) subscription to Firmus' $2.9 billion equity raising, once Firmus lists on the ASX?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The amount NVIDIA invests and the equity stake it holds in Firmus Technologies after its preference shares convert to ordinary equity at Firmus' ASX IPO.\",\n   \"period\": \"Firmus' ASX listing later in 2026 (preference shares convert to ordinary equity there); the stake is already undertaken, so it is also tracked by its amount at NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, expected early 2027). Set from the item's 'later this year' listing timing, within 18 months of the 2026-07-08 item.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-12\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the spot rental price of an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute average over calendar 2026, after peaking around $3.20/hour in May 2026 and then declining?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The realized spot rental price for an hour of H100 GPU time over calendar 2026, versus the ~$3.20/hour May 2026 peak.\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (check date 2026-12-31); set from the item's reported May-2026 peak (~$3.20/hour) and subsequent decline in the H100 spot-rate series.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-13\",\n   \"question\": \"What will happen to HBM/DRAM contract prices over the 12 months to mid-2027, after rising roughly tenfold over the past year and becoming the data-center bottleneck?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The change in HBM/DRAM contract prices over the 12 months to mid-2027, versus the roughly tenfold rise over the prior year.\",\n   \"period\": \"The 12 months to 2027-06-30 (next calendar year); set from the item's report that memory prices rose tenfold over the past year and its view that conditions will persist absent an HBM breakthrough.\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-14\",\n   \"question\": \"Will France's competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU markets and issue a decision (fines or remedies) by Nvidia's fiscal year-end 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"A final decision by the French competition authority on its antitrust probe into Nvidia's cloud-AI and GPU practices.\",\n   \"period\": \"2027-01-31 (Nvidia's current fiscal year-end; set because the item reports a pending regulatory decision 'nearing a conclusion' with no date of its own)\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"X-15\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will U.S. federal agencies obligate in AI-related spending in calendar/fiscal 2026, and how much in new AI-related contract awards will be recorded?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The total AI-related spending obligated by U.S. federal agencies in 2026 (reported at $7.2 billion so far, versus $675 million in 2024) and the value of potential AI contract awards (reported at $91.8 billion, versus $4.6 billion in 2024).\",\n   \"period\": \"Calendar/fiscal 2026; settled by year-end 2026 U.S. federal procurement data (e.g., USAspending.gov) reporting total AI-related obligations and contract awards. Set from the item's 2026 obligations figure ($7.2 billion) and potential-awards figure ($91.8 billion).\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  }\n ],\n \"Y\": [\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-1\",\n   \"question\": \"How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed under its AI-cloud programme by its next annual report?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The amount of NVIDIA's credit-support obligations under the announced AI-cloud programme.\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2027-02-28, year FY2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 4 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-2\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2027-07-01, year 2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 1 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-3\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping its Rubin-generation platform by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2026-12-31, year 2026\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-4\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Calendar 2026 data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2027-03-31, year 2026\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 12 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-5\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Calendar 2027 data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2028-03-31, year 2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 12 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-6\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue growth be in FY2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA total revenue growth in FY2027\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2027-02-28, year FY2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 12 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-7\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue growth be in FY2028?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA total revenue growth in FY2028\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2028-02-29, year FY2028\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 12 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-8\",\n   \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA stand-alone CPU sales\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2027-02-28, year FY2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 14 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-9\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA launch the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by 2027-12-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether NVIDIA launches the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by the end of 2027.\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2027-12-31, year 2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 25 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-10\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA complete its proposed investment in Firmus Technologies’ preference-share raising by 2026-12-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA’s proposed investment in Firmus Technologies\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2026-12-31, year 2026\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-11\",\n   \"question\": \"Will China authorize Alibaba, ByteDance, and DeepSeek to buy NVIDIA H200 chips by 2027-01-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"China authorization for named AI firms to purchase NVIDIA H200 chips\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2027-01-31, year 2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"article 37 of the packet\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"system_id\": \"Y-12\",\n   \"question\": \"How much incremental compute capacity will Google, Amazon, Meta, and Microsoft add in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Aggregate incremental compute capacity added by Google, Amazon, Meta, and Microsoft\",\n   \"period\": \"due 2028-03-31, year 2027\",\n   \"opened_from\": \"an article outside the 40\"\n  }\n ]\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 45 -B 8 '同一题、续期，还是另一题' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 45 -B 8 '同一题、续期，还是另一题' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"302-<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n303-<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n304-<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n305-<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n306-</ul>\n307-\n308-<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n309-<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n310:<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n311-<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n312-\n313-<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n314-<ol class=\"steps\">\n315-<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n316-<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n317-<li><b>能核对</b>有一个日期和一份公开材料能把答案放进事先固定的档吗？没有就重写问题。到期没有材料记\"未能判定\"，不算错。</li>\n318-<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n319-</ol>\n320-<p>另外三条写法检查<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1、5、6 条</span>。没过的问题不能照原样开，要重写；重写不了就不开，材料作证据。</p>\n321-<ul>\n322-<li><b>原文支持：</b>主体、量或事件、时间依据都能在原文找到。原文没给日期、而规则允许研究员定检查日的，用那个日期并标明：没写日期的待决监管事项用本财年末（第 3 节 E 类）；还没签的约束性义务用文章后 18 个月以内能核对签约的那天<span class=\"src\">D185、D210</span>。不把\"拟议\"\"预计\"写成\"已签\"\"已完成\"。</li>\n323-<li><b>口径完整：</b>算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚；支出、融资、担保、订单、收入不混。</li>\n324-<li><b>时间正确：</b>原文支持这个期间，不把几年的平均写成今年。</li>\n325-</ul>\n326-\n327-<h3>不开的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 的清单</span></h3>\n328-<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n329-<thead><tr><th>不开</th><th>出处</th><th>它变成什么</th></tr></thead>\n330-<tbody>\n331-<tr><td>季度数字和季度指引</td><td>第 1 版 §6；PRD 06 梯子第 6 条</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n332-<tr><td>同一段指引里的每一行（\"费用率、税率是模型输入，不是争论\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n333-<tr><td>没日期的\"护城河\"\"战略\"</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n334-<tr><td>高管任免、股东投票、回购授权；章程</td><td>第 1 版 §6；章程出自 D239 选定的 role-v29 原文（\"executive appointments, shareholder votes or bylaws\"）</td><td>证据或不留</td></tr>\n335-<tr><td>例行诉讼程序</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n336-<tr><td>客户的部署计划（\"它是供应商需求和产品问题的证据，除非改变供应商自己的现金或信用风险\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据；改变公司自己的现金或信用风险时按 C 类判</td></tr>\n337-<tr><td>以约束性义务为理由开：公司自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。它们不是约束性义务；对别的问题仍可以是证据，或按别的开题理由判</td><td>D236、D238</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n338-<tr><td>把远期年度预测改装成事件</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n339-<tr><td>后年及以后的年度量（约束性义务除外）</td><td>PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；D185</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n340-<tr><td>同一个量的另一个估计、另一种口径、另一个来源</td><td>第 1 版 §6 测试 4</td><td>那个已开问题的证据，由匹配并入</td></tr>\n341-</tbody></table></div>\n342-\n343:<h3>同一题、续期，还是另一题：匹配这一步的事，抽取不判库里的</h3>\n344-<ul>\n345-<li><b>总规则：</b>同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</li>\n346-<li><b>同一题：</b>同一个结果能同时判两个问题。另一个估计、来源、措辞、方向<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 测试 4</span>；同一总量的另一种人群或代用口径（D190 碰撞裁决提示 collision-v1：\"another population or proxy of one aggregate\"；D197 引的 role-v12 原文：\"another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\"）。候选并进已开问题，用它的结果档和到期日<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。只有以共同量理由开题、带量的候选由代码自动判，其余是匹配和碰撞裁决的判断。</li>\n347-<li><b>同一个计划的几种说法</b>（担保、融资承诺、信用支持……），最后核对的是同一个数，是一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。</li>\n348-<li><b>同一件事的不同截止日：</b>早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据，不另开；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上并进来的证据，不等新文章<span class=\"src\">D248 第 2 条</span>。</li>\n349-<li><b>同一代产品的几个里程碑：</b>一题，问能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；送样、发布作证据；会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span>。</li>\n350-<li><b>公司自己的量：</b>只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据，两种年份差得多时分量低一点<span class=\"src\">D248 第 4 条；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</span>。</li>\n351-<li><b>身份：</b>事件和政策题里模型写的期间起点，不拿来挡合并；对象、事件、截止日照旧核对<span class=\"src\">D248 第 5 条</span>。</li>\n352-<li><b>续期：</b>同一个量或同一串事件的下一个期间<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Succession、D190</span>。</li>\n353-<li><b>另一题：</b>同一件事里答案能分开走、分析员会分别下注的：有自己驱动的组成部分；同一笔交易或同一份附注里两个各自会变、分别盯着的数；另一件事<span class=\"src\">D190 碰撞裁决的四种；D248 第 1 条收窄了\"担保和融资\"</span>。</li>\n354-<li><b>约束性义务：</b>\"一笔或一个计划\"一题<span class=\"src\">D210</span>；一笔交易是不是某个已按金额开题的计划的一部分，由匹配判，是就并入<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。还没签的单笔交易是\"签不签\"的是非题，照旧可以开，不并进计划的金额题<span class=\"src\">D210；PRD 06；D248 未改</span>。</li>\n355-<li><b>共同量：</b>以共同量理由开题、带量的候选（量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算），由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判同一题；政策阶段和别的事件保留按事件判的身份；不带这个开题理由的主题量由模型判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>。</li>\n356-</ul>\n357-\n358-<h3>谁判，谁查</h3>\n359-<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n360-<thead><tr><th>内容</th><th>谁</th></tr></thead>\n361-<tbody>\n362-<tr><td>测试 1–3、同一篇文章里的测试 4、属于哪一类、问题怎么写</td><td>抽取的模型（判断）</td></tr>\n363-<tr><td>结果档形状、期间是真日期、到期在文章之后、季度数、年限、约束性义务 18 个月、<code>settled_by</code> 不为空</td><td>代码：只查形状，不判重要性<span class=\"src\">D154、D155、D184</span></td></tr>\n364-<tr><td>和库里的同一题、续期、另一题</td><td>匹配（Jev）和碰撞裁决<span class=\"src\">D190</span>；共同量由代码<span class=\"src\">D197</span></td></tr>\n365-</tbody></table></div>\n366-<p class=\"note\">年限按公司财年数：2026 年 7 月时 NVIDIA 在 FY2027（2027 年 1 月结束），所以 FY2028 是明年。代码原来按自然年算，把 FY2028 当成后年拒掉；在 v29 答案的 40 个带年份的候选里拒错了 2 个。已修，测试是 <span class=\"path\">tests/test_fiscal_year_horizon.py</span><span class=\"src\">D243</span>。</p>\n367-\n368-<h2 id=\"evidence\"><span class=\"num\">5</span>证据标准</h2>\n369-<h3>5.1 留的规则和四类</h3>\n370-<blockquote><p><b>一个在追这家公司的分析员，读到会在本周笔记里写下来，因为它让某个问题的答案更可能或更不可能。</b>问题不限于库里已有的，也不限于本公司：客户、供应商、竞争者、监管、宏观都算<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2；D208 七类驱动</span>。</p></blockquote>\n371-<p><b>整体倾向谨慎，对增量敏感。</b>杂音很大，不是什么都要抽，不是什么都算线索。判一句话之前先问：这是新信息吗？它让哪个问题的答案变了？一件新发生的事、一个新数字、一个新的具体判断，是增量，不能漏；重复常识、描述长期状况、泛泛的看法，是杂音<span class=\"src\">D243</span>。增量和杂音的具体界线按 5.3 各行和边界一起判<span class=\"src\">D250</span>。</p>\n372-<p>从第一段读到最后一段，分析员会记的（按本节和 5.3 各行边界一起判）都留。一页有八条就是八条，不挑<span class=\"src\">D199</span>。它们通常是下面四类之一；四类描述的是会记的陈述长什么样，不是\"属于四类就一定留\"，留不留由上面的规则判；具体不留的行和边界见 5.3。</p>\n373-<ol class=\"steps\">\n374-<li><b>公司自己的数字、指引或决定</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"同店销售本季增长 4.2%\"；\"管理层把全年收入指引定在 120–130 亿美元\"；\"董事会批准 100 亿美元回购\"；\"公司取消软件订阅费，生产使用免费\"<span class=\"src\">Alex 判 8，Omniverse</span>。</li>\n375-<li><b>客户、供应商、竞争者、伙伴的有规模、有日期或有名字的动作，以及它们公布的数字</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2：三者有一个就够</span>第 1 版的例子\"Google Cloud 季度收入 248 亿美元，增长 82%，积压超过 5000 亿美元\"<span class=\"src\">Alex 判 11</span>；\"最大客户说明年订单砍五分之一\"；\"主要供应商说 2027 年产能翻倍\"；\"对手在欧洲降价 15%\"；\"一家银行选用竞争对手的系统\"；\"一家软件公司把本公司的模型集成进政府系统\"。后两条有名字、没金额，也留<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。</li>\n376-<li><b>具名一方的主张或估计</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"CFO 说十年前建的工厂仍满负荷\"；\"分析师把明年 EPS 预期上调到 4.10 美元\"；\"做空机构指控公司虚增应收 20 亿美元\"；\"内存厂说 2027 年短缺最严重，持续到 2030\"。</li>\n377-<li><b>政策或监管的决定或步骤</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"监管机构批准该药第二个适应症\"；\"政府要求该产品出口须申请许可\"；\"25 家公司联名反对过早限制开放权重模型\"；\"财长说将调查某国公司是否窃取知识产权\"。</li>\n378-</ol>\n379-<p><b>典型的主张和背景</b><span class=\"src\">D243 第 5 条</span>：Alex 的原话是\"这种典型的主张背景属于常识，基本上抽出来也没有太多的意义除非带数字和具体的叙事不然都是属于不采纳\"。常识，就是跟这家公司的分析员读这篇之前就已经知道的：谁领先、谁在竞争、需求强、供给紧、融资难这类说法，和对已知状况的重述。这类陈述没有数字和具体的叙事就不收。不是常识的，是新信息，比如一份新报告的判断、一个新的市场数据、刚发生的事的细节，照上面的规则判，分析员会记就留。</p>\n380-<ul>\n381-<li><b>常识，不收：</b>\"博通 CEO 说能从英伟达抢份额\"；\"Blackwell 和 Rubin 仍然供不应求\"；\"融资会是扩大算力最大的障碍\"；\"内存厂避开了以往的产能过剩\"；\"博通预计明年随着新客户推出定制芯片大幅增长\"。</li>\n382-<li><b>新信息，收：</b>一位科技公司高管对媒体说\"中国国产 AI 芯片厂商已经全部卖光，客户在考虑性能更低的芯片\"；\"旧型号 GPU 的租金在涨\"；研究机构说\"这让 Rubin Ultra 暂时没有成熟的扩展方案，给对手留出了空间\"；\"华为现在占中国 AI 芯片市场约一半，这个市场约 500 亿美元\"。</li>\n383-<li><b>有数字也要过上面的规则：</b>作者说\"英特尔多年领先，占 CPU 市场 59%\"，和英伟达的问题关系不大，分析员不会记。</li>\n384-</ul>\n385-\n386-<h3>5.2 不完整也是证据</h3>\n387-<p>预测、传闻、反证、远期、条件情景都是证据；它们的层级和确定性另记。不因为\"还没发生\"\"不是官方\"\"离现在远\"\"和我们方向相反\"就不留；一个真实的反例可能比十个顺风数字更重要<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>。有名有姓的动作缺金额、缺日期也是证据，分量可以低一点<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。不留清单只按 5.3 各行和边界删，不能用来删掉标准要留的陈述：\"a reject rule never removes what the standard keeps\"<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。</p>\n388-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"matter\":\"M01\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"X-1\"],\"note\":\"Tracks the programme’s commitments through December 2027 rather than at the FY2027 annual report.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M01\",\"system\":\"Y\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"Y-1\"],\"note\":\"\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M02\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"note\":\"X-1 tracks the programme’s total amount, not whether the Ohio guarantee is signed.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M02\",\"system\":\"Y\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"Y-2\"],\"note\":\"Uses an earlier 2027 deadline.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M03\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"X-6\"],\"note\":\"\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M03\",\"system\":\"Y\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"Y-4\"],\"note\":\"\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M04\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"X-8\"],\"note\":\"Opened from an article outside the 40.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M04\",\"system\":\"Y\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"Y-5\"],\"note\":\"\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M05\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"X-7\"],\"note\":\"Uses the reported 2028 alternative deadline rather than the end of 2027.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M05\",\"system\":\"Y\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"Y-9\"],\"note\":\"Asks about launch rather than customer shipments.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M06\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"X-4\"],\"note\":\"Opened from an article outside the 40.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M06\",\"system\":\"Y\",\"status\":\"narrower\",\"ids\":[\"Y-11\"],\"note\":\"Names three companies rather than Chinese companies generally.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M07\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"X-3\"],\"note\":\"Opened from an article outside the 40.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M07\",\"system\":\"Y\",\"status\":\"opened\",\"ids\":[\"Y-3\"],\"note\":\"Opened from an article outside the 40.\"}\n{\"matter\":\"M08\",\"system\":\"X\",\"status\":\"missed\",\"ids\":[],\"note\":\